    "Scouting Notes": "Very mediocre defender at first. \n Profile is entirely based on the fact that he has 70 grade power. \n He's a massive human being, and extremely strong.\n That strength gives him the bat speed and raw juice to make up for the lack of momentum his body is unable to generate.\n Whiffs and K's were a *huge* issue in AAA\n Given his athletic profile, it's a big positive how often he is able to elevate the ball. Posting very low GB%. \n Though a high infield popup rate does bring a bit of concern, as those are basically auto outs, along with his strikeouts, that's a lot of auto outs.\n He has the raw and game power to be a 1B or DH in MLB. It's a matter of whether he can get the bat to ball enough for it to matter.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/23/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Very mediocre defender at first. \n Profile is entirely based on the fact that he has 70 grade power. \n He's a massive human being, and extremely strong.\n That strength gives him the bat speed and raw juice to make up for the lack of momentum his body is unable to generate.\n Has shown some struggles against breaking balls with a lot of chases/whiffs, however it has taken a step in the right direction in 2022.\n Walks a lot. Strikeouts not as bad as you might expect given the profile.\n Given his athletic profile, it's a big positive how often he is able to elevate the ball. Posting very low GB%. \n Though a high infield popup rate does bring a bit of concern, as those are basically auto outs.\n He has the raw and game power to be a 1B or DH in MLB. It's a matter of whether he can get the bat to ball enough for it to matter.\"",
